{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790966572,"nonce":"yXFMvlYYaC8Ld08PBALBecuDHe0=","message":"Landed as 726ce68560050bbc24e6bbc4bccbc8090b6149f8.\n- ashui.reactive.Watch: calls react at creation and at each LayoutTree.flush where read() changed; flush polls watches before applying queued writes, so reactions run outside Blinc's graph and may build and remove elements. Polled each flush, so read() is a computed get.\n- ashui.ui.Show(when, then, ?otherwise): a box holding the branch for its condition; each branch built under its own child Owner (Owner now takes an explicit parent) and disposed on a switch.\n- ashui.ui.For(each, item): a box with one item per value; an item still present (==) keeps its element, removed ones are disposed, order set with replaceChildren. ComputedDynamic exposes version so a recompute returning the same array still reconciles.\n- hxx: \u003cif {cond}\u003e..\u003celse\u003e..\u003c/if\u003e is a Show, \u003cfor {v in list}\u003e..\u003c/for\u003e a For; a signal or computed condition or list is read; a body of several elements is wrapped in a Div; loop variables are typed while lowering the body.\nBoth are boxes in the layout: Taffy 0.6 has no display: contents.\nSmoke (41 checks, interp/hybrid/jit): branch swap with relayout reported; For builds 3, drops one and reuses the rest (no rebuild), builds only the new item.","files":null}]}